759	\section{Conclusion}
760	In this study, we develop SAR-RWKV, a speckle-suppression network that couples sparse attention with an RWKV backbone to denoise SAR imagery. We build a sparse-gated spatial-mixing RWKV module that combines a Top-K sparse-selection mechanism with the global-modeling capability of RWKV to extract key features efficiently, strengthening global modeling and effectively suppressing over-smoothing during denoising. To better recover texture detail, we design an AFM module that maps features into the frequency domain via the DCT and adaptively weights multi-band information through a content-aware frequency-gating mechanism, sharpening the modeling of texture and edge detail. To better balance denoising against texture preservation, we design an AFF module that achieves adaptive co-expression of spatial and frequency features. Overall, SAR-RWKV shows superior performance in both quantitative and qualitative evaluations, indicating that the proposed sparse-attention-based RWKV framework has good application potential for SAR image denoising. Nevertheless, the experiments show that the proposed algorithm performs slightly worse on the ENL metric; future work will therefore aim to further improve denoising capability while balancing denoising against texture preservation, so that the model can achieve better visual results.
