708	\subsection{Model Stability Test}
709	To probe how robustly SAR-RWKV performs across diverse scenes, we drew 100 images at random from the Sentinel-1 dataset—mirroring the protocol of \cite{ref36}—denoised them with our algorithm and the nine comparison algorithms, and averaged the three objective metrics, as reported in Table 10. SAR-RWKV attains the best values on both EPD-ROA and UM, indicating that it has both better texture preservation and better overall denoising performance. Although SDUDNet and FRANet attain the best and second-best ENL, their EPD-ROA values indicate poor edge preservation; the other two methods with higher ENL, G-MONet and ACGNet, also suffer from poor edge preservation. In summary, the proposed algorithm can balance speckle suppression against texture preservation.
